<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santander, Spain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santander is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-biscay">Bay of Biscay</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabria">Cantabria</a>. A medieval fishing and trading town, it grew in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>'s port for wool and the colonial trade. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a> it fell to Nationalist and Italian forces in August 1937, isolating the remaining Republican north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santander-spain.jpg" alt="Santander, Spain" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noreenlam · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Palacio_de_la_Magdalena_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
